'' T40, RUN: a maths intrinsic -- sqr, abs, int, fix, frac, sgn, exp, log, atn, atan2 --
'' over a UDT with no operator of that name and a numeric 'operator cast' is the
'' intrinsic of the converted value, as fbc gives it. Check left the call untyped, so
'' 'print sqr( f )' printed nothing, and the lowering declined, so 'dim r as double =
'' sqr( f )' read garbage. Over casts to long AND string the numeric one is taken; a
'' single cast stays single; atan2 converts either argument. Output identical to
'' fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/math-udt-cast.bas -o tests/codegen/mathudtcast.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/mathudtcast.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/mathudtcast.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1.58113883008419
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3.75-4-3-0.75-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 9-1 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 12.18249396070347 0.9162907318741551 1.190289949682532
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2.58113883008419 0.3805063771123649-1.080839000541168
